Panic where a thread's worker fails to start

A worker whose script fails to load or parse fires an error event at the
worker and never runs the thread it was given, so the thread's joiner
waits forever and nothing tells why. The spawning thread panics on that
event, as it does where the browser refuses to construct the worker, and
the panic reaches the page like any other.

